{
 "note": "Cape Naturaliste Lighthouse (1903-04), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), the inHerit record and Lighthouses of Australia. A squat 20 m round tower of local limestone, painted white, a moulded concrete gallery with an iron balustrade, a cast-iron Chance lantern (about 4.3 m across) with a domed cap. The round tower is approximated by stacked boxes (two crossed bars and a square per tier, narrowing upwards), so it reads as a twelve-sided stepped column; a proper round tower and lantern want a Blender layer. The 1973 brick power house just east of it is the outbuilding. Metres: x left (west-south-west) to right (east-north-east) as seen from the south-south-east (the path up from the cottages and car park), y back.",
